| Shared Database, Shared Schema | All tenants in one DB, tenant_id column | Cost-efficient | Data isolation risk | SMB customers |
| Shared Database, Separate Schema | One DB, schema per tenant | Moderate isolation | Schema migration complexity | Mid-market |
| Separate Database | Database per tenant | Strong isolation | Higher cost, ops complexity | Enterprise |

## Tenant Isolation Requirements
- [ ] **Data Isolation**: Tenant A cannot access Tenant B's data (enforced at DB + app layer)
- [ ] **Performance Isolation**: Tenant A's load doesn't impact Tenant B (rate limiting, resource quotas)
- [ ] **Security Isolation**: Tenant A's breach doesn't affect Tenant B (separate encryption keys)
- [ ] **Configuration Isolation**: Tenant A's settings independent of Tenant B (tenant-specific configs)

