### Enterprise User Stories

**US-ENT-001: Single Sign-On (SSO) with SAML**
As an enterprise IT administrator
I want employees to log in using our corporate identity provider
So that we centrally manage access and enforce security policies

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] SAML 2.0 support (Okta, Azure AD, OneLogin compatible)
- [ ] SP-initiated and IdP-initiated flows
- [ ] Attribute mapping (email, name, role)
- [ ] Just-in-Time (JIT) provisioning (auto-create user on first login)
- [ ] SCIM support for user provisioning/deprovisioning (optional)
- [ ] Admin can configure via UI (upload metadata XML)

**US-ENT-002: Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)**
As an enterprise account owner
I want granular permission management
So that users only access what they need (principle of least privilege)

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Predefined roles: Owner, Admin, Member, Viewer
- [ ] Custom roles: Define permissions per resource type
- [ ] Permission inheritance: Workspace → Project → Resource
- [ ] Audit trail: Log all permission changes
- [ ] UI: Permission matrix for easy configuration

**US-ENT-003: Audit Log Export for Compliance**
As a compliance officer
I want to export all user activity logs
So that I can prove compliance during audits

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Searchable audit log UI (filter by user, action, date range)
- [ ] Export formats: CSV, JSON, SIEM-compatible
- [ ] Tamper-proof logs (cryptographic signatures)
- [ ] Retention: Configurable (1 year default, up to 7 years)
- [ ] Includes: User ID, action, timestamp, IP, resource affected, old/new values

